  "finding": "The original roughly 12% increase is not reproduced when the embedded native compiler source is held constant. The hash-fixed host is faster in all three CPU pairs; both hosts produce byte-identical images and identical checker/IR traces. There is no observed loss of output deduplication or structural sharing. The original pair also compiled a changed linker implementation into its native image, and has a larger output. Do not interpret these saturated-host repeats as precise attribution of every original CPU-second.",
